WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.122
Hi! A kitten is a living thing, and a stone is not. But what about a seed, or a mushroom? Today let's review living and non-living things from Primary 3.

2
00:00:13.272 --> 00:00:17.274
Living things need air, food and water to stay alive.

3
00:00:17.424 --> 00:00:23.394
Living things grow. A chick grows into a hen, and a seed grows into a tree.

4
00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:30.522
Living things reproduce, making young ones of their own. Birds lay eggs, and plants make seeds.

5
00:00:30.672 --> 00:00:38.682
Living things respond to changes around them. A touch-me-not plant folds its leaves when touched, and plants grow towards light.

6
00:00:38.832 --> 00:00:48.618
Many living things can move by themselves. Non-living things, like a stone or a toy car, do not have these characteristics.

7
00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:55.602
Plants can be flowering plants, like the sunflower, or non-flowering plants, like ferns and mosses.

8
00:00:55.752 --> 00:01:05.322
Animals include mammals, birds, fish, insects, amphibians and reptiles. An insect has 6 legs and 3 body parts.

9
00:01:05.472 --> 00:01:11.946
Fungi, like mushrooms and the mould on bread, are not plants, because they cannot make their own food.

10
00:01:12.096 --> 00:01:17.850
Bacteria are so small that we need a microscope to see them.

11
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.178
Watch out! You can't tell if something is living just by whether it moves!

12
00:01:23.328 --> 00:01:28.626
A car moves, but it does not grow or reproduce, so it is not a living thing.

13
00:01:28.776 --> 00:01:35.826
A tree can't walk, but it grows, reproduces and needs water, so it is a living thing.

14
00:01:35.976 --> 00:01:43.698
Your turn! Is a mushroom a plant? Pause and think.

15
00:01:43.848 --> 00:01:52.050
No. A mushroom is a fungus. It cannot make its own food. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:52.200 --> 00:02:03.690
Another one! An animal has 6 legs and 3 body parts. Which group does it belong to? Pause and think.

17
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:13.386
It's an insect, like an ant or a butterfly. A spider has 8 legs, so it is not an insect. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:13.536 --> 00:02:26.370
Next one! Bread left out for several days grows a fuzzy layer on top. What is it, and which group of living things is it in? Pause and think.

19
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:35.274
It is mould, which is a fungus. It feeds on the bread, because it cannot make its own food. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:35.424 --> 00:02:44.922
Last one! A robot can walk and talk. Is it a living thing? Pause and think.

21
00:02:45.072 --> 00:02:53.466
No. A robot does not need food, does not grow and cannot reproduce. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:53.616 --> 00:03:04.266
Remember: living things need air, food and water, they grow, reproduce and respond to changes. Check all the characteristics, not just whether it moves.

23
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:09.690
Living things are grouped into plants, animals, fungi and bacteria.

24
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.882
Next time you go out, how many groups of living things can you spot?

